.Dd October 14, 2026
.Dt XFT_ALLOC 3
.Os xft
.Sh NAME
.Nm xft_arena_allocator ,
.Nm xft_gpa_allocator ,
.Nm xft_reporta_allocator ,
.Nm xft_page_allocator ,
.Nm xft_alloc_clone
.Nd allocator interface
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In alloc.h
.Ft t_allocator
.Fn xft_arena_allocator "t_arena *arena"
.Ft t_allocator
.Fn xft_gpa_allocator "t_gpa *gpa"
.Ft t_allocator
.Fn xft_reporta_allocator "t_reporta *gpa"
.Ft t_allocator
.Fn xft_page_allocator void
.Ft t_buffer
.Fn xft_alloc_clone "t_any self" "t_buffer buffer"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
Every xft container that owns memory takes a
.Vt t_allocator
by value and calls through its vtable.
A
.Vt t_allocator
pairs a table of function pointers with an untyped pointer to the backend
state:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
typedef void     (*t_free)(t_any alloc, t_buffer old);
typedef t_buffer (*t_reallocate)(t_any alloc, t_buffer old,
                     t_size new_size, t_size align);
typedef t_buffer (*t_allocate)(t_any alloc, t_size size,
                     t_size align);
typedef void     (*t_destroy)(t_any alloc);
typedef t_buffer (*t_clone)(t_any self, t_buffer buffer);

typedef struct e_alloc_vtable {
	t_free        free;
	t_reallocate  realloc;
	t_allocate    allocate;
	t_destroy     destroy;
	t_clone       clone;
} t_alloc_vtable;

typedef struct s_allocator {
	t_alloc_vtable  vtable;
	t_any           allocator;
} t_allocator;
.Ed
.Pp
The
.Fa alloc
argument of
.Fa allocate ,
.Fa realloc ,
.Fa free
and
.Fa destroy
is the
.Fa allocator
member.
The
.Fa self
argument of
.Fa clone
is a pointer to the
.Vt t_allocator
itself.
All five types are declared
.Ql nonnull
on their first argument.
.Pp
Allocations are
.Vt t_buffer
fat pointers.
A failed allocation is signalled by a
.Dv nullptr
.Fa mem
member; the
.Fa size
member may still be nonzero, so test
.Fa mem .
On success
.Fa size
is the usable size, which may be larger than requested.
A buffer handed back to
.Fa free
or
.Fa realloc
must be the
.Vt t_buffer
exactly as it was returned, since some backends use its
.Fa size
to find where it belongs.
.Pp
A
.Vt t_allocator
does not own its backend state.
The arena, GPA or report allocator passed to the constructor must outlive
every copy of the returned
.Vt t_allocator ,
and is released only by calling
.Fa destroy
or the backend's own destroy function.
.Pp
.Fn xft_arena_allocator ,
.Fn xft_gpa_allocator ,
.Fn xft_reporta_allocator
and
.Fn xft_page_allocator
build a
.Vt t_allocator
around one backend.
They allocate nothing and are declared
.Ql const .
The vtable entries map onto the backends as follows:
.Bl -tag -width "xft_reporta_allocator"
.It Fn xft_arena_allocator
.Fa allocate
calls
.Fn xft_arena_alloc
and returns a buffer of exactly
.Fa size
bytes.
.Fa realloc
always allocates a new block of
.Fa new_size
bytes, copies the smaller of the old and new sizes, and leaves the old block
in place.
.Fa free
does nothing.
.Fa destroy
calls
.Fn xft_destroy_arena .
See
.Xr xft_arena 3 .
.It Fn xft_gpa_allocator
.Fa allocate ,
.Fa realloc ,
.Fa free
and
.Fa destroy
call
.Fn xft_gpa_alloc ,
.Fn xft_gpa_realloc ,
.Fn xft_gpa_free
and
.Fn xft_gpa_destroy .
See
.Xr xft_gpa 3 .
.It Fn xft_reporta_allocator
As above with the
.Fn xft_reporta_*
functions.
.Fa destroy
prints a usage report to standard error.
See
.Xr xft_gpa 3 .
.It Fn xft_page_allocator
.Fa allocate ,
.Fa realloc
and
.Fa free
call
.Fn xft_palloc ,
.Fn xft_palloc_resize
and
.Fn xft_palloc_free ;
.Fa align
is ignored.
.Fa destroy
is
.Dv nullptr .
The
.Fa allocator
member points to a static
.Vt t_page_alloc
that carries no state.
See
.Xr xft_palloc 3 .
.El
.Pp
All four set
.Fa clone
to
.Fn xft_alloc_clone .
.Pp
.Fn xft_alloc_clone
treats
.Fa self
as a
.Vt "t_allocator *" ,
allocates
.Fa buffer Ns .size
bytes through its
.Fa allocate
entry with an alignment of
.Fa buffer Ns .size
rounded up to a power of two, and copies
.Fa buffer Ns .size
bytes from
.Fa buffer Ns .mem
into the new block.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
The constructors return the filled
.Vt t_allocator .
.Pp
.Fn xft_alloc_clone
returns the new buffer as returned by the backend, so its size may exceed
.Fa buffer Ns .size .
On failure it returns a buffer with
.Fa mem
set to
.Dv nullptr
and
.Fa size
set to 0.
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
#include <xft.h>

__attribute__((__nonnull__(1), __noreturn__))
void	xft_main(const t_any *const __restrict__ sp)
{
	t_gpa		gpa;
	t_allocator	allocator;
	t_buffer	memory;
	t_buffer	copy;

	(void)sp;
	gpa = xft_new_gpa();
	if (gpa.slab == nullptr)
		xft_exit(1);
	allocator = xft_gpa_allocator(&gpa);
	memory = allocator.vtable.allocate(allocator.allocator, 1000, 64);
	if (memory.mem == nullptr)
	{
		allocator.vtable.destroy(allocator.allocator);
		xft_exit(1);
	}
	xft_pin_invariant(memory.size >= 1000);
	copy = allocator.vtable.clone(&allocator, memory);
	if (copy.mem != nullptr)
		allocator.vtable.free(allocator.allocator, copy);
	allocator.vtable.free(allocator.allocator, memory);
	allocator.vtable.destroy(allocator.allocator);
	xft_exit(0);
}
.Ed
